From: Tuth <tuth3378@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:58:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/24] MS2000: THE recreate-storm root cause - dispatch read
 entries[pc+1] (one displacement)

THE ROOT CAUSE, proven by hexdump of the generated trampoline:

  4D 8B 44 D0 08   =   mov r8, [r8 + rdx*8 + 8]

The execUntilCycles dispatch load was written as
  m_asm.mov(g_funcToCall, asmjit::x86::ptr(g_funcToCall, g_funcArgGPs[1], 3, 8));
intending scale=3 and access size=8 - but asmjit's 4th mem operand argument is
the DISPLACEMENT. The generated loop read entries[pc + 1] instead of entries[pc].

Consequences, all measured:
- For every pc inside a multi-word block, entries[pc+1] is the block's own
  interior mark &funcRecreate. The bootstrap dispatch at P:0xFF0000 loaded its
  own block's interior mark and called funcRecreate(0xFF0000) forever:
  the ~75k/s destroy+re-emit storm (pre makeRoom-fix), 4+ GB asmjit pool
  (retired code never released while the trampoline stayed entered), warden
  kills, and after the makeRoom abort-fix a ~2.4 billion/run no-op livelock
  with zero boot progress.
- Every "phantom funcRecreate from the table with no writer" observation fits:
  the writers wrote the marks to pc+1; the instruments watched pc. The cell
  hexdump/direct-read comparison (directCell vs loaded) closed it.

THE FIX: ptr(base, index, 3) - no displacement. Jitmem::makePtr's 4th argument
IS a size (the execLoop uses it correctly); only the raw asmjit::x86::ptr call
in execUntilCycles had the displacement. (PERF-DSP-2, my own code.)

AFTER (bankstorm, 30 s run, warden 4096 MB):
- t= lines RETURN: boot advances, t=4.53/5.53/6.53 s heartbeat, DSP executes
  the real firmware in low P (PC=0003D7/000521/00012E, SR=C00150/C00049),
  H8S<->DSP traffic alive (SHI words in 139K, TX frames 264K, RX overruns 0),
  JIT healthy (chains=1, blocks=271, codeMB=0.27), ~2x real-time.
- recreates=15 TOTAL per run (was: billions) - the surviving ones are the
  legitimate mid-block entry at P:0xFF001A (the MS2k "upload stage-1, reconfigure
  memory, jump back to bootloader" flow) doing exactly what recreate was
  designed for: split once, continue.
- Memory flat. No warden kill.

Also in this commit (instruments, all capped/rate-limited): honest ASM
funcRecreate-compare trace (materialized imm64 - cmp r64,imm64 does not exist),
baked base/index globals, direct-cell read, generated-code hexdump, cell write
log with thread ids, makeRoom starts-here abort (kept - it is correct defense:
a block that starts at _pc is valid for _pc, destroyToRecreate skips it for the
same reason), hot-entry forced block boundaries, chain/block/recreate counters.

Next, separate bug (known from the H-bank session): at t~6.5 s the bankstorm
program change drives the DSP to the wild pc 0x800010 (valid 24-bit P address,
unmapped physical page); the legitimate recreate there hits bad_alloc in the
memory model and terminates the host. The window guard passes because 0x800010
< sizeP(0x1000000); the fix belongs in the memory model / wild-pc handling.
